The key insight (this is important)

Your host is acting like a router between multiple isolated domains:

physical LAN (10.0.0.0/24)
Docker DMZ (172.16.10.0/24)
Docker internal (10.1.0.0/24)
VMware networks (192.168.x.x)


# What does: " docker exec -it "  actually do?

When you run:

	> docker exec -it p-web-02 bash

You are saying:

“Start a shell process INSIDE that container’s namespaces.”
	no SSH server needed
	Docker injects the process directly

