     or best professional method : use dockerfile so install nesessary tools and buils the image after 
    in dockerfile: there is screen shot explain also 
    
   # Assume your current image is called:
    	my_kali_image
	First create a directory:
		> mkdir kali-upgrade
		> cd kali-upgrade
	Create a file named exactly:
		Dockerfile
	Put this inside:

   		 FROM my_kali_image
   		 
   		 RUN apt-get update && \
    		     apt-get upgrade -y && \
    	             apt-get clean && \
    	             rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/
    	             
    	Then, from the kali-upgrade directory, run in the terminal:
    		> docker build -t my_kali_image:v2 .  #The . means:  "Use the current directory as the build context."
    		
    		my_kali_image       ← old version (backup)
		my_kali_image:v2    ← upgraded version
	

	
